network_blocks.py, darknet.py, and yolo_pafpn.py were copied from the existing
Megvii-derived model sources in the local RemingtonVision project. Their
copyright notices are retained.

Modified for Part Tracking Demo UALR in 2026:
- yolo_head.py retains the stock inference layers and parameter names, and
  removes training losses, assignment, visualization, and optional imports.
- yolox.py retains the backbone/head inference composition and removes
  training and visualization entry points.
- __init__.py provides a validated CPU/FP32 model factory and applies the
  recorded activation and BatchNorm settings supplied by the caller.

The resulting graph emits raw YOLOX box channels and sigmoid objectness/class
probabilities. It does not include preprocessing, training, non-maximum
suppression, checkpoint deserialization, or device-control code.
